# runify-bmad-first

Default for **runify.icu**: product thinking, planning, specs, tickets, and multi-file implementation **go through BMad skills**, not ad-hoc chat execution.

## No heavy assumptions (all models)

**MUST NOT** infer product, scope, roles, or data rules from chat vibe or old docs without **asking the user to confirm** when the answer changes build behavior.

When unsure: **one clear question** beats a detailed guess. The user prefers to answer and guide.

Record confirmed decisions in BMad memlog / spec — not silent reinterpretation.

## Opt-out

If the user clearly says **no bmad**, **skip bmad**, **just do it in chat**, or similar — follow their request for that turn only.

## When the user "throws things" at you

**Do not** treat chat as the system of record. **Do not** write or expand provisional docs in `_bmad-output/initiative-runify-icu/` (`product-brief-runify.md`, `stack-proposal.md`, `CANONICAL.md`) as a substitute for BMad.

Instead, in the **first reply**:

1. Acknowledge what they said (one short paragraph).
2. Name the **one BMad skill** to run next and **why**.
3. Give a **copy-paste invoke line** (skill name + 1–2 sentences of intent).
4. Offer **`bmad`** only if they need routing help.

Stay in **intake/coach mode** until they invoke the skill or opt out. Small factual answers (one line, no planning) are OK without redirect.

## Routing table

| User intent | Skill | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Vague, many options, "help me ideate" | **`bmad-brainstorming`** | Diverge; many ideas on a topic |
| One fuzzy product, stress-test assumptions | **`bmad-forge-idea`** | Converge; act or drop one idea |
| Unsure the product is worth building | **`bmad-prfaq`** | Working Backwards challenge |
| Clear enough to describe the product | **`bmad-product-brief`** | Formal brief under `_bmad-output/.../brief-*/` |
| Stack / technical spine (locked stack already agreed — capture in architecture) | **`bmad-architecture`** | After brief or with spec |
| Distill into buildable spec | **`bmad-spec`** | Kernel + companions; references locked stack |
| Epics / stories / board | **`bmad-ticket`** | After spec |
| Screens / flows | **`bmad-ux`** | When UI matters |
| Code change | **`bmad-build`** | Per ticket or small scoped ask |
| "What next?" / setup / initiative | **`bmad`** | Hub |
| Research external facts | **`bmad-deep-recon`** | Not for stack re-decision |
| Repo agent rules block | **`bmad-project-context`** | After spec stabilizes |

## Artifact lifecycle (no duplication)

Read `_bmad-output/initiative-runify-icu/ARTIFACT-LIFECYCLE.md`.

Files marked **`provisional-pre-bmad`** MUST be **removed or archived** once the matching BMad output exists. **Do not** maintain parallel chat-born and BMad-born versions.

## Stack locks during ideation

Tech stack for runify.icu is **agreed** (see provisional `CANONICAL.md` / `stack-proposal.md` until BMad architecture + spec absorb them). During **`bmad-forge-idea`** / **`bmad-brainstorming`**, do not re-open stack unless the user explicitly asks.

## Harness paths

- Skills: `.agents/skills/`
- Output: `_bmad-output/initiative-runify-icu/` (active initiative)
- Agent index: root `AGENTS.md`
